then I do design, then I do training, then I do deploy, and then I do basically governance throughout the whole thing.", "text_chars": 345, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "c92aa561-d4f9-48c4-b3ef-b8f99359db5d", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789366961.255751, "updated_at": 1789366969.920729, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "text": "Almost. You skipped **build** and **test**.\n\nThe clean rail is:\n\n**Handoff → Validate → Plan → Design → Build → Test → Train → Deploy**\n\nAnd then **Governance + Health/Commercial** run across the entire lifecycle.\n\nSo your first part was good: MHI sales/solution architecture hands you the sold scope and solution package; you validate the documentation, requirements, assumptions, dependencies, risks, provisioning, timeline, stakeholders, and ask whatever questions you need.\n\nThen you convert that into the executable plan, refine the solution design, assign/build the workstreams, test it, train the users, and only then deploy to production.\n\nThat’s the exact kind of correction I want us doing in reps.", "text_chars": 708, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "40ecb38c-66ce-4fe8-8e6e-6c1cf38eff2b", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1789366961.2730405, "updated_at": null, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "model_editable_context", "part_kinds": [], "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "1165440d-99ff-4c1e-8456